{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffSize","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLStaffSize"}],"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLStaffSizeV","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLStaffSize","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"struct","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"title":"MXLStaffSize","roleHeading":"Structure"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffSize\/init(value:scaling:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffSize\/scaling","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffSize\/value"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffSize\/Equatable-Implementations"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations","title":"Default Implementations"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"]]},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SH","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The staff-size element indicates how large a staff space is on this staff, expressed as a percentage of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"work’s default scaling. Values less than 100 make the staff space smaller while values over 100 make the staff"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"space larger. A staff-type of cue, ossia, or editorial implies a staff-size of less than 100, but the exact"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value is implementation-dependent unless specified here. Staff size affects staff height only, not the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"relationship of the staff to the left and right margins."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLStaffSize"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In some cases, a staff-size different than 100 also scales the notation on the staff, such as with a cue"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"staff. In other cases, such as percussion staves, the lines may be more widely spaced without scaling the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"notation on the staff. The scaling attribute allows these two cases to be distinguished. It specifies the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"percentage scaling that applies to the notation. Values less that 100 make the notation smaller while values"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"over 100 make the notation larger. The staff-size content and scaling attribute are both non-negative decimal"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"values."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps the MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<staff-size>"},{"type":"text","text":" element."}]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstaffsize"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStaffSize/value":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffSize\/value","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"value","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","preciseIdentifie